# AI Assisted:
From: TicWatch Pro 5 port
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: icc-rpm: enable real RPM voting (Step C)

Reverts the stub from `icc-rpm-novote.patch` so qnoc-monaco votes to the RPM for
real again (clk_set_rate of the bus clocks + msm_rpm_send_message for
master/slave BW + QoS).

Correction of the root-cause analysis (Step A-2): the "vendor" that was compared
(t5-gki-kernel, Winkmoon) is NOT the monaco vendor -- it is a generic GKI
5.15.202 WITHOUT qnoc monaco, without slate and without drivers/rpmsg/rpm-smd.c.
The REAL monaco vendor (mobvoi/mobvoi-ticwatch-kernel and
rcky844/android_kernel_mobvoi_monaco) uses EXACTLY our same path:

  - drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c: practically identical to ours (only
    licenses/EXPORT_SYMBOL and the tag mapping in aggregate differ).
    Both call qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send_msg() -> msm_rpm_send_message()
    (drivers/rpmsg/rpm-smd.c), NOT qcom_rpm_smd_write() (smd-rpm).
  - drivers/clk/qcom/clk-smd-rpm.c: also votes with msm_rpm_send_message() in
    BOTH trees. That is: in our kernel the clocks "that work" use the SAME API
    as the ICC. There is no "smd-rpm path that works".

Therefore there is NO smd-rpm port to do: the only functional difference is the
stub. This patch just removes it. Apply ONLY for the Step C experiment (boot with
`boot console` + capture-consola + crashlog and see where it dies).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
---

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpm.c
@@ -108,14 +108,6 @@
  */
 int qcom_icc_rpm_set(struct icc_node *src, struct icc_node *dst)
 {
-	/* dace bring-up: do not send votes to the RPM. The hard crash to EDL
-	 * after the ICC nodes of qnoc-monaco register points at RPM voting
-	 * (icc_set_bw -> qcom_icc_rpm_set -> qcom_icc_rpm_smd_send). With this
-	 * stub the drivers get their paths (deferred resolved, eMMC alive)
-	 * without touching the RPM; the bus keeps the rates the bootloader left
-	 * (enough for bring-up). Remove once RPM voting is debugged. */
-	return 0;
-#pragma message("dace: qcom_icc_rpm_set STUB (no RPM voting)")
 	struct qcom_icc_provider *qp;
 	struct qcom_icc_node *qn;
 	struct icc_node *n, *node;
